From: Juraj Oršulić <juraj.orsulic@fer.hr>
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: defer NVPCF notifications only in fine-grained mode

RmDeferNvpcfNotifyIfIdle(), added by open-gpu-kernel-modules pull
request #1299, takes the dynamic power mutex without checking the power
management mode first. rm_acpi_nvpcf_notify() calls the new function
before os_ref_dynamic_power(nv, NV_DYNAMIC_PM_FINE), which returns
before it locks the mutex or takes a power reference when the configured
mode is coarse or NV_DYNAMIC_PM_NEVER. rm_init_dynamic_power_management()
selects NV_DYNAMIC_PM_NEVER when it fails to create the mutex, and leaves
the mutex NULL, so in that case an NVPCF notification would dereference
NULL.

Return NV_FALSE in both modes, so that rm_acpi_nvpcf_notify() keeps its
existing path there and delivers the notification right away.

---
diff --git a/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c b/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c
index c999c92..d5e6837 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/arch/nvalloc/unix/src/dynamic-power.c
@@ -1532,7 +1532,14 @@ NvBool RmDeferNvpcfNotifyIfIdle(
     nv_priv_t *nvp = NV_GET_NV_PRIV(nv);
     NvBool bDefer;
 
-    if (nvp == NULL)
+    /*
+     * Defer only when os_ref_dynamic_power(nv, NV_DYNAMIC_PM_FINE) would
+     * take the mutex and could resume the GPU. In coarse mode it does
+     * neither. In NV_DYNAMIC_PM_NEVER mode the mutex can be NULL, because
+     * rm_init_dynamic_power_management() selects that mode when it fails
+     * to create the mutex.
+     */
+    if ((nvp == NULL) || (NV_DYNAMIC_PM_FINE > nvp->dynamic_power.mode))
     {
         return NV_FALSE;
     }
